## Approach

Wrap the inner `Ephemeris` in `Arc` at the FFI boundary so handles are refcounted. Add `swisseph_share(handle)` that clones the `Arc` and returns a new opaque pointer. `swisseph_free` becomes a refcount drop — the last drop frees the engine. All 61 existing handle-dereference sites (`&(*handle).0`) continue to work identically because the `Arc` transparently derefs to `Ephemeris`.

This is a purely FFI-layer change — `swisseph` (the Rust crate) doesn't change. `Ephemeris` is already `Send + Sync` by construction (pinned in `tests/send_sync.rs`), so wrapping it in `Arc` is sound.

## Files

- **Modify**: `swisseph-ffi/src/lib.rs` (lines ~21, ~117-162) — change `SweEphemeris` from `(Ephemeris)` to `(Arc<Ephemeris>)`, update `swisseph_new` to wrap in `Arc`, rewrite `swisseph_free` to drop the `Arc`, add `swisseph_share`
- **Modify**: `swisseph-ffi/Cargo.toml` — bump version `0.1.0` → `0.2.0`
- **Regenerate**: `swisseph-ffi/include/swisseph.h` — `cbindgen` (header freshness test will fail otherwise)
